# 創刻のアテリアル with message:UseAntiFont 0, set with `option smooth-text off` on SC0000's first page: natively 設定's
# ﾒｯｾｰｼﾞ tab (文字の縁をなめらかにする), on the port the options panel's ﾒｯｾｰｼﾞ section. OK applies it at once
# (text_set_use_anti_font@0x414d80, the text manager's +0x548), and later text is drawn from GGO_BITMAP glyphs.
#
# With it 0, the builders draw through text_draw_string_primary_or_ruby, which starts the string at the effect
# offset, and both publishers move each glyph object that is not ruby back by the offsets in effect mode 3, so the
# text sits where antialiased text does (TextRules.PublisherMovesAliasedEffectGlyphs; docs/engine-re.md, "AntiFont
# off in 4.33G and 4.38D"). History's renderer moves its glyphs the same way. Himegari's 4.24J has no such move: its
# text lands one pixel right and down (himegari-antifont-off.steps).
#
# Run on a fresh sandbox, on both targets, and compare the shots:
#   py -3.11 -X utf8 tools/drive.py --game arterial native start
#   py -3.11 -X utf8 tools/drive.py --game arterial native run tools/drive/scenarios/arterial-antifont-off.steps
#   py -3.11 -X utf8 tools/drive.py --game arterial native stop

rand-seed 13
wait 5
click adv.next
wait-state script=TITLE timeout=90
wait 6
click title.start
wait-state top=SC0000@0xfff timeout=90
settle timeout=20
shot arterial-antifont-page1            # antialiased

option smooth-text off                  # clears message:UseAntiFont, then OK
wait 1
dialogs                                 # none
expect top=SC0000@0xfff

advance
state
shot arterial-antifont-off-page2        # aliased, in its place
advance
state
shot arterial-antifont-off-page3

move adv.next
wheel up                                # History redraws the pages, aliased from page 2 on
wait 1.5
settle
shot arterial-antifont-off-history
